<title>CHINA: DAH SING INTERIM NET RISES 39.7 PERCENT.</title>
<headline>DAH SING INTERIM NET RISES 39.7 PERCENT.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended June 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   145.0	vs 109.0</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    51.0	 vs 41.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  0.066 loss vs 0.805 loss</p>
<p>    Net			    348.50     vs 249.49</p>
<p>    Company name		 Dah Sing Financial Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  August 25-29</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   September 1</p>
<p>NOTE - Dah Sing provides banking and related financial services.</p>
<p>Comparative figure has been reclassified to conform with current year's presentation.</p>
<p>The exceptional items for the current period and last corresponding period represent loss on disposal of fixed assets and long-term investments.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
